# Word of Command (CR 723.2, 107.3a, 119.4, 601.2d, 733.1-2) on a wide board (15 creatures: Bot1's Terror and six Memnites, Bot2's eight Memnites): Fire Covenant's X is paid in
# life, so Bot1 may announce 16 at 18 life with three lands. Dividing all 16 on Terror of the Peaks would cost Bot2 3 life
# more than it has left, so that attempt is reversed. Made again, the same division is refused (`~`: an answer the question
# could not leave out, a division), and with the 16 on Bot2's own Memnite it is cast. Deciding
# whether the divided-targets question still has a live answer tries the divisions one at a time (`required::alive`), so it
# is no slower for the 15 creatures.

